### COAir API — runnable examples
###
### Works in VS Code (REST Client extension) and JetBrains HTTP Client.
### Run them top to bottom: the login response feeds every later request.
### Equivalent curl for each call is in the comment above it.

@host = https://your-api-host.example.com
@username = replace-me
@password = replace-me
@projectId = paste-a-project-id-from-step-11


### 1. Health — no auth. Confirms you can reach the API at all.
# curl -s $host/api/health
GET {{host}}/api/health


### 2. Log in. Everything below reuses {{login.response.body.access_token}}.
# curl -sX POST $host/api/auth/login -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
#   -d '{"username":"...","password":"..."}'
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}


### 3. Who am I — validates a stored token on app boot.
# curl -s $host/api/auth/me -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 4. List every account, with usage and billing state.
GET {{host}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 5. Create a metered (demo-plan) customer account.
POST {{host}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "acme",
  "password": "choose-a-strong-one",
  "display_name": "Acme Ltd",
  "role": "user",
  "token_limit": 2000000,
  "features": { "correspondence": true },
  "plan_type": "demo",
  "initial_credits": 1000,
  "markup_percent": 30,
  "storage_limit_bytes": 30000000000
}


### 6. Update it. Omitted fields are left alone; `features` replaces the whole map.
PATCH {{host}}/api/admin/users/acme
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "display_name": "Acme Construction Ltd",
  "token_limit": 5000000,
  "features": { "correspondence": true, "provider_compare": true }
}


### 7. Top up credits. `credits` is signed; a negative value claws back.
### Reuse the same idempotency_key on a retry and it will not double-credit.
POST {{host}}/api/admin/users/acme/credits
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "credits": 250,
  "reason": "Pilot extension agreed 2026-08-12",
  "idempotency_key": "acme-topup-2026-08-12"
}


### 8. Zero the token counters (credits and storage are untouched).
POST {{host}}/api/admin/users/acme/reset-usage
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 9. Global spend against the configured budget.
### remaining_pct is a fraction (0.9982), not a percentage.
GET {{host}}/api/usage
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 10. Billing breakdown. All four filters are optional.
GET {{host}}/api/admin/usage?username=acme&date_from=2026-08-01&date_to=2026-08-31
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### === Company SuperAdmin walkthrough ===
### Log in as a company owner (an ordinary account whose org role is `owner`);
### everything below is then scoped to that company automatically.

### C1. Which company am I, and what may I do in it?
GET {{host}}/api/org
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### C2. My company's users.
GET {{host}}/api/org/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### C3. Create a user inside my company.
### role / plan / credits / quota are NOT accepted here — they come from the
### company policy. Only `correspondence` and `provider_compare` are assignable.
POST {{host}}/api/org/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "site-surveyor",
  "password": "choose-a-strong-one",
  "display_name": "Site Surveyor",
  "features": { "correspondence": true }
}


### C4. My company's projects — including ones I never joined.
GET {{host}}/api/org/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### C5. Who can reach one project.
GET {{host}}/api/org/projects/{{projectId}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### C6. Grant that user access to a project.
### A username outside my company answers 422 user_not_in_organization.
PUT {{host}}/api/org/projects/{{projectId}}/members/site-surveyor
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "editor" }


### C7. Revoke it again.
DELETE {{host}}/api/org/projects/{{projectId}}/members/site-surveyor
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### C8. Promote someone to co-SuperAdmin (or demote with "member").
### You cannot change your own role, and the last owner cannot step down.
PATCH {{host}}/api/org/users/site-surveyor
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "org_role": "owner" }


### === Platform operator: creating a company ===

### P1. Create the company and appoint its SuperAdmin in one call.
### The account must already exist (step 5 above).
POST {{host}}/api/admin/orgs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Acme Ltd",
  "owner_username": "acme",
  "default_plan_type": "demo",
  "default_credits": 1000,
  "default_token_limit": 2000000,
  "project_limit": 10,
  "allow_member_projects": false
}


### P2. Every company, with member and project counts.
GET {{host}}/api/admin/orgs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### P3. Act inside a customer's company. Operators only — the header is ignored
### when anyone else sends it.
GET {{host}}/api/org/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Org-ID: paste-an-org-id-from-P2


### P4. Attach an existing project to a company. Answers 409 with the offending
### usernames when its members are not all in that company; add ?force=true only
### once you have resolved them.
POST {{host}}/api/admin/orgs/paste-an-org-id/projects/{{projectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 11. Projects. An admin sees every project; this is the source of project ids.
GET {{host}}/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 12. A content endpoint — note the extra header.
### Without X-Project-ID this returns 428 project_required.
GET {{host}}/api/library
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Project-ID: paste-a-project-id-from-step-11


### 13. Deactivate an account (soft delete → is_active=false, data retained).
DELETE {{host}}/api/admin/users/acme
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 14. Superadmin only — create another operator.
### An `admin` caller gets 403 superadmin_required:create_operator.
POST {{host}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ops2",
  "password": "choose-a-strong-one",
  "display_name": "Second Operator",
  "role": "admin"
}
